From b277732348f26c6d0e2646ebe1dc8d463466945a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:24:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DiskCache: a format version of the fork's own

The disk cache key is the format version, the host features and the
codegen-affecting config; it does not name the FEX build. eac-2610
changed codegen in several places (POPF's flag handling, IRET with NT,
...) but kept upstream's version 30, so a cache filled by one fork build
was taken by the next one (and by an upstream FEX-2610 with the same
codegen config): blocks translated before a fix kept running without it.
The guest's Steam FEX tool runs with DiskCache=1.

FormatVersion is now 0x8000 | revision << 8 | upstream version (0x811E):
bit 15 is never set upstream, so fork and upstream caches never mix, and
every fork change to codegen increments the revision (reset to 1 on a
rebase onto a new upstream version). This one invalidates every cache
written so far, once.

InstructionCountCI updated with ninja instcountci_tests /
instcountci_update_tests: BinaryCacheVersion everywhere, and the POPF and
POP SS entries that the fork's flag changes had left stale (40 -> 43,
22 -> 25; 32-bit and FlagM variants likewise). 108/108 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
